# ARCANA auth secrets. Copy to .env.auth beside it, fill in, chmod 600.
#
# NEVER commit the filled-in file, and never inline these values in a systemd
# unit: units ARE committed, and git history is permanent. This example exists
# so that a new machine can be configured at all — the key names are not the
# secret, and a machine nobody can configure is the same class of problem as a
# repository that is not the whole record of what runs.

# Signing key for the user-facing JWTs.
AUTH_JWT_SIGNING_KEY=

# The shared key for machine-tier calls between services, sent as
# X-Internal-Key. Anything holding this can ask a service to act without a user.
INTERNAL_API_KEY=

# Operator wallet ADDRESSES for the admin tier (seasons, competitions).
#
# Addresses, never private keys. The guard compares this list against the wallet
# SIWE recovered from a signature the user made in their own wallet, so the list
# grants no ability to sign anything — it only names who may act once they have
# already proved who they are.
#
# The addresses are public on chain. What is worth not publishing is the
# ASSOCIATION between them and ARCANA, which is why the filled-in file stays out
# of git while this example goes in.
AUTH_ADMIN_WALLETS=
